  "assumptions": [
    "Simplified simulation: no air resistance, flat ground, ball launched from ground level.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down; horizontal speed stays constant. Landing distance = speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8, computed exactly.",
    "A hit is a landing within 1.5 m of the target centre, both edges counted. The ball is drawn with a 1.2 m radius for visibility but treated as a point; its drawn centre sits 1.2 m above the path.",
    "Every flight is shown over 2 seconds of screen time, so the flight-time readout differs from what you see. Reset restores the first target, the score, the trails and the default settings.",
    "Real balls are slowed by air and land shorter, especially at high speed; the 45° best angle is exact only without air resistance."
  ],
